### User Story 2 - Phone Number Registration and Login Acceptance Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost/api

### 1. Register new user (success)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "userName": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "coverImage": "https://example.com/avatar.jpg",
  "biography": "This is a test user"
}

### Expected: 201 Created with accessToken, refreshToken, and user info

###

### 2. Register with duplicate phone number (409 conflict)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "userName": "Another User",
  "email": "another@example.com",
  "password": "password456"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict - Phone number already exists

###

### 3. Register with invalid phone number (400)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "invalid-phone",
  "userName": "Test User",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Invalid phone number format

###

### 4. Login with correct credentials (success)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with accessToken, refreshToken, and user info
### Save the accessToken and refreshToken for next tests

###

### 5. Login with wrong password (401)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - Invalid credentials

###

### 6. Login with non-existent phone number (401)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886999999999",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - Invalid credentials

###

### 7. Get user profile with valid token (success)
# Replace {{accessToken}} with the token from login/register
GET http://localhost/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected: 200 OK with user profile (userId, phoneNumber, userName, email, etc.)

###

### 8. Get user profile without token (401)
GET http://localhost/api/me

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

###

### 9. Get user profile with invalid token (401)
GET http://localhost/api/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token-here

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - Invalid or expired token

###

### 10. Refresh token (success)
# Replace {{refreshToken}} with the token from login/register
POST http://localhost/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with new accessToken and new refreshToken
### Save the new tokens

###

### 11. Try to use old refresh token again (401 - rotation test)
# Use the OLD refreshToken from step 10
POST http://localhost/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{oldRefreshToken}}"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - Token should be revoked after rotation

###

### 12. Refresh with invalid token (401)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "invalid-refresh-token"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

###

### 13. Register with phone number containing separators (normalization test)
POST http://localhost/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886-912-345-679",
  "userName": "User With Dashes",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: 201 Created - Phone number should be normalized to E.164

###

### 14. Login with normalized phone number
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345679",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - Should work with normalized format

###

### 15. Rate limit test for login - Multiple rapid requests (429)
# Send this request 6+ times rapidly to trigger rate limit
POST http://localhost/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886912345678",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: After 5 requests within 60 seconds, should return 429 Too Many Requests

###

### 16. Rate limit test for register - Multiple rapid requests (429)
# Send this request 6+ times rapidly to trigger rate limit
POST http://localhost/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "+886900000001",
  "userName": "Rate Limit Test User",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Expected: After 5 requests within 60 seconds, should return 429 Too Many Requests

###

### Notes:
### - Phone number format: E.164 (e.g., +886912345678)
### - Access token expires in 3600 seconds (1 hour)
### - Refresh token expires in 2592000 seconds (30 days)
### - Refresh token rotation: old token becomes invalid after refresh
### - Rate limit: 5 requests per 60 seconds for /auth/register and /auth/login
### - All timestamps are in UTC with ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2026-01-30T12:34:56Z)
